title: 'Decision: Option A (async deep-link + poll) for agent-purchase personhood gate'
summary: 'Locked Option A as the MVP handoff for agent-initiated purchases: agent initiates -> server mints a World ID connect URL -> agent surfaces it to the human -> human completes Selfie Check in World App -> backend verifies proof -> purchase proceeds; agent polls for status. Goal: prove the flow end-to-end with a MOCK verifier first, then do UX/bells-and-whistles (storefront polish, Chrome-extension surface, MCP docs) over the week. Grounded in World ID docs research that confirmed the connect-URL seam.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#checkout-route'
  - '#merchant-mcp'
  - ^personhood-verified
  - $agent-purchase-flow
  - ^checkout-authorized
decisions:
  - id: D-handoff-option-a
    decision: Use Option A (async deep-link + poll) for the agent-initiated selfie handoff, verified first with a mock verifier; UX polish, Chrome-extension surface, and MCP docs come later in the week.
    rationale: World ID's own flow produces a 'connect URL' (QR/deep link) that is exactly the out-of-band artifact an agent can hand to the human, so A is the natural fit; it also gives the strongest per-purchase proof and the most compelling demo. Prove-then-polish keeps us unblocked.
  - id: D-selfie-widget-hosting
    decision: MVP surfaces the World ID connect URL directly from the agent/MCP (print/QR); the Chrome-extension-hosted IDKit widget is a later polish option, not MVP.
    rationale: Fastest path to a working demo; the extension is really a 'where the widget lives' choice and can be added without changing the server contract.
learnings:
  - World ID 'Selfie Check' is a real Beta credential (liveness+uniqueness from a selfie), alongside Proof of Human (Orb) and Document Check.
  - 'World ID verification is client-widget-driven via IDKit: frontend gets an RP signature from its backend (signing key), builds an IDKit request (app_id, rp_id, action), which produces a ''connect URL'' -> QR on desktop / deep link into World App on mobile -> human completes in World App -> returns a ZK proof (proof, nullifier, issuer_schema_id).'
  - Backend verifies by forwarding the payload to POST https://developer.world.org/api/v4/verify/{rp_id}. This verify step is exactly what our mock verifier stands in for.
  - There is NO documented headless/server-initiated selfie flow — verification requires a human-facing widget + the World App. That constraint is the feature working as intended (personhood), and the connect URL is the seam that lets an agent hand off to the human.
  - 'Real integration will later require: a registered app in the World Developer Portal (app_id/rp_id), a server-side signing key to mint RP signatures, and the /api/v4/verify call — all skipped by the mock.'
tags:
  - design
